B.cUm=new A.d8("bookreader","A bespoke BOOK-PAGE reader for one row's Markdown text: parchment ground, a drop capital on the opening paragraph, thin ink rules between sections, oxblood links and serif typography (display + body). Read only \u2014 it never writes the row. A DROP-IN UPGRADE for a `readOnly` `notepad`: the binding (`table`/`rowId`/`column`), the `onLinkTap` contract and `jumpToSectionSetting` all behave identically, and the SAME block grammar parses the text, so swapping the type keeps the applet's data flow. Dark mode is a deliberate night-reading treatment (deep warm ground, soft ink), not an inverted page. The node bounds its own size, so an unbounded host axis renders a real page rather than a blank one.",B.bLY,!1)
B.doX=new A.q("model",B.U,'The anatomy model: { parts: [{ id, name, group, kind: "muscle"|"bone", layer: "superficial"|"deep", color (hsl(...) or #hex), info, from, to, points: [[x,y,z],..], radii: [start, belly, end], peak, segments, ring }], groups: [..], title, subtitle, center: [x,y,z], tilt, yawStep, disclaimer }. A part with several strands may use `tubes: [{points, radii, ..}, ..]` instead of the inline points/radii. A malformed model renders an honest empty state \u2014 it never crashes the applet.',B.f,null)
B.dd_=new A.q("disclaimer",B.C,'Honesty line shown under the info card. Defaults to "Schematic model \u2014 simplified for learning, not a medical reference."; an empty value falls back to that default rather than hiding the line. (The model\'s own `disclaimer` key takes precedence.)',B.f,null)
B.d5n=new A.q("initialYaw",B.ah,"Opening spin in degrees, snapped to the model's step (default 30).",B.f,null)
B.d62=new A.q("rotationStep",B.ah,'Degrees per yaw/pitch step the viewer OPENS on: 5, 15 (default, or the model\'s own `yawStep`) or 45. The viewer offers all three in its "\u22ef" cluster; a value it does not offer falls back to the model.',B.f,null)
B.d7l=new A.q("sensitivity",B.U,"AUTHOR LEVER for gesture sensitivity \u2014 the standard `sensitivity` attribute shared by every bespoke surface. Either a per-channel object, { rotate, pan, zoom, scroll, tapSlop, longPress }, or a single number as shorthand for the four continuous channels. Each value is a MULTIPLIER on the node's own calibration, clamped to 0.25-3.0; higher means the surface reacts to less input. A USER's pick in the viewer's Sensitivity sheet always outranks this, per channel, and declaring nothing leaves behavior exactly as calibrated. The tapSlop and longPress channels are additionally floored for accessibility (12px, 300ms) whatever is declared.",B.f,null)
B.d5h=new A.q("minZoom",B.ah,"Minimum zoom factor (default 0.4).",B.f,null)
B.dhG=new A.q("maxZoom",B.ah,"Maximum zoom factor (default 4).",B.f,null)
B.dgY=new A.q("showList",B.W,"Show the grouped part-list drawer and its toolbar button (default true).",B.f,null)
B.d9p=new A.q("features",B.U,"DECLARATIVE CHROME GATES. { probe, dissect, deepLayer, movements, pivot, snapView, sensitivity } \u2014 each defaults to true, and only the literal `false` turns one off, so an undeclared (or malformed) value leaves the node byte-identical to the full study toolbelt bodytomy ships. A gate removes ENTRY POINTS (the chips and the tap tool), never the model or the painter: `dissect: false` also drops the Hide tap tool, the card's Hide chip and the Undo/Redo/X-ray trio, and a stored `hide` tap mode falls back to rotate rather than stranding the user in a mode whose exit was removed. For an applet that mounts the body only to PICK on it (see `moveset`), all seven off leaves turn/tilt/zoom, tap-to-select and the parts list.",B.f,null)
B.ddJ=new A.q("selectionTable",B.ay,'Opt-in TWO-WAY selection mirror. Declared, the node writes one row per highlighted structure into this table IN PICK ORDER (a full replace, never a merge) and adopts that table back as its highlight set \u2014 so the rest of the applet can act on what the user picked with stock list/filter nodes, and an action that writes the table (e.g. "show this exercise\'s targets") lights the figure up. Undeclared, the node stays board-free: it renders a model, it never touches a row. Column names default to partId / name / group / pickOrder and are overridable via `selectionIdColumn`, `selectionNameColumn`, `selectionGroupColumn`, `selectionOrderColumn`.',B.f,null)
B.dn7=new A.q("selectionIdColumn",B.v,'Part-id column of `selectionTable` (default "partId").',B.f,null)
B.drm=new A.q("selectionNameColumn",B.v,'Resolved part-name column (default "name").',B.f,null)
B.daU=new A.q("selectionGroupColumn",B.v,'Resolved group column (default "group").',B.f,null)
B.dp6=new A.q("selectionOrderColumn",B.v,'Zero-based pick-order column (default "pickOrder"); the read-back sorts on it, so the figure and the list always agree on order.',B.f,null)
B.bkr=s([B.doX,B.dd_,B.d5n,B.d62,B.d7l,B.d5h,B.dhG,B.dgY,B.d9p,B.ddJ,B.dn7,B.drm,B.daU,B.dp6],t.G)
B.cTR=new A.d8("anatomy","A schematic, rotatable 3D anatomy viewer. Parts are tube meshes built from a few control points and a belly-radius profile; the view is orthographic with the spin locked to fixed steps, so each distinct view is projected and depth-sorted once and cached in a small LRU (pan, zoom and roll are pure 2D and never reproject). THREE AXES: drag sideways to spin (yaw), up/down to tilt (pitch), twist with two fingers to roll; two-finger drag pans and pinch or scroll zooms. Tap a part for a plain-language card, which can always be collapsed to a chip. The deep-layer toggle peels the superficial parts. Geometry is DATA: the whole model lives in `model`, so a new body region ships as JSON.",B.bkr,!1)
B.dmk=new A.q("table",B.ay,"Bubbles table (one row per idea).",B.f,null)
B.deb=new A.q("filter",B.U,'Opt-in row scope: { "column": <col>, "value": <val-or-token> } keeps bubbles whose column equals the value; the set form { "column": <col>, "in": [..] } keeps rows whose value is in the set. Tokens resolve live: $selected:<table> \u2192 the selectRow pick, $rowId \u2192 the injected host row, $playerId \u2192 the current player. Absent \u2192 all rows; present but the resolved value is empty (e.g. nothing selected) \u2192 no bubbles, never all. Links auto-scope to the visible bubbles.',B.f,null)
B.dgp=new A.q("scopeColumn",B.v,"Opt-in ENGINE scope filter (see `BoardState.rowsForScoped`) \u2014 the same convention the `explorer` node's `scopeColumn` reads via `activeScope`, so a bubl bound to a scoped table (e.g. a File > Board > bubbles chain) shows only the open file/board's bubbles even when no ancestor explorer for that hop happened to mount. Distinct from `filter` (a token-resolved value/set filter); the two may combine. Absent = unchanged behavior.",B.f,null)
B.doF=new A.q("labelColumn",B.v,'Text label column (default "label").',B.f,null)
B.diY=new A.q("labelFallbackColumn",B.v,"When the label is empty, show this column's first line instead (e.g. a titleless comment's text).",B.f,null)
B.diA=new A.q("sublabelColumn",B.v,'Optional second, smaller line under the label \u2014 a quantity or status ("2 L", "low", "out").',B.f,null)
B.d7e=new A.q("computeColumn",B.v,"Auto-compute: a numeric attribute (e.g. calories) that an output bubble SUMS across its inputs (following the links); a stated value that differs from the sum is flagged as an unaccounted gap.",B.f,null)
