B.dkV=new A.q("zoomable",B.W,"With holdMenu: a zoom chip focuses INTO a bubble \u2014 the board shows its children, water taps spawn inside it, and a breadcrumb chip zooms back out (default off).",B.f,null)
B.dlN=new A.q("duplicable",B.W,"With holdMenu: a duplicate chip copies the held bubble AND everything nested inside it (its whole sub-tree) plus every link that stays within the copy; the new copy is offset from the original (default off).",B.f,null)
B.dbN=new A.q("selectStyle",B.W,"Tap a bubble to SELECT it: a floating in-canvas style bar (fill, shape, outline colour + thickness, rename, subtext, resize, erase) \u2014 each control writes a per-bubble style column, so appearance is user-chosen, not enum-driven (default off).",B.f,null)
B.dkQ=new A.q("pinchZoom",B.W,"Pinch-zoom + pan the whole board: two fingers pinch to zoom (0.5\xd7\u20133\xd7) and drag to pan; a trackpad two-finger scroll pans and \u2303/\u2318 + wheel zooms (the draw-tool model). One-finger gestures keep their meanings (default off).",B.f,null)
B.dfb=new A.q("showNested",B.W,"Show bubbles nested inside others at the ROOT level (default on). Off: nested bubbles tuck behind their parent \u2014 which wears a +N badge \u2014 and zooming INTO a bubble still reveals its contents.",B.f,null)
B.d88=new A.q("collapsedColumn",B.v,'Opt-in per-row FOLDER state: any bubble with hierarchy children (parentColumn or nestLinkType) shows a small expand/collapse chip; collapsing folds its whole descendant subtree \u2014 and every link touching a hidden bubble \u2014 behind a "+N" badge (same visual as showNested\'s badge). Set \u2192 toggling WRITES this bool column (like posColumn persists position), so the fold survives a reload. Unset \u2192 the chip still works, but the fold is SESSION-ONLY (in-memory), no schema change needed. PRECEDENCE with showNested: the two compose by OR \u2014 a bubble is hidden if either applies. showNested off already tucks every nested bubble away by default; a per-bubble collapse folds a SPECIFIC subtree on top of that (or entirely on its own with showNested on, for fine per-bubble control instead of an all-or-nothing default). Absent (default) \u2192 the chip still appears on any bubble with children, but nothing is ever pre-folded, so an untouched board renders unchanged.',B.f,null)
B.da5=new A.q("arrowCollapsedColumn",B.v,'Opt-in per-row FOLDER state for the DOWNSTREAM ARROW CASCADE \u2014 a SECOND, independent collapse axis from [collapsedColumn] (which folds NESTED children). A bubble flagged true in this bool column folds its whole downstream chain: every bubble reachable by following OUTGOING links (linksTable, linkFrom\u2192linkTo, drawn-arrow edges only, never nesting edges), behind a "+N" badge (same visual as collapsedColumn\'s). Cycle-safe (arrow graphs can loop). V1 hides the WHOLE downstream cascade \u2014 a bubble reachable from a collapsed root hides even if a still-visible bubble also points to it; shared-node-aware hiding is a deliberate follow-up, not an oversight. Composes with collapsedColumn and showNested by OR (any applicable rule hides a bubble). No built-in chip this round \u2014 toggle via the existing toggleField function against this column. Absent (default) \u2192 zero behavior change.',B.f,null)
B.dla=new A.q("multiSelect",B.W,"With selectStyle: select MANY bubbles at once \u2014 drag on open water for a marquee, shift-click to add, ctrl/cmd-click to toggle (add or remove). While more than one is selected, style changes apply to all and a drag moves the whole group (default off).",B.f,null)
B.df4=new A.q("holdMultiSelect",B.W,"With multiSelect: long-hold a bubble then tap others to extend the selection one at a time (add-mode), instead of marquee/shift/ctrl-click only. Also extends holdMenu's long-press to add a link's endpoints to the selection (default off).",B.f,null)
B.doS=new A.q("fillColorColumn",B.v,'Column holding a per-bubble fill "#RRGGBB" (soft look). Empty = the palette default.',B.f,null)
B.dlU=new A.q("fillColorMap",B.U,'Opt-in DERIVED fill colour for read-only consumers with no colour column: { "column": <col>, "colors": { <value>: <ramp-name-or-#hex>, .. }, "default": <ramp-name-or-#hex>? }. Resolved AFTER fillColorColumn \u2014 a literal per-row hex from that column always wins when both are set. Absent/unmapped with no default = unchanged.',B.f,null)
