$.fwG=function(){var s="bd_wikipick_seedmap",r=t.N,q=t.z
return A.a([A.y(["id","st_wsm_engine_choice","board",s,"x",0,"y",-260,"width",340,"text","(a) RENDER ENGINE: recommend the existing canvas-with-connections node (bublee/wireframe's, per canvas-connection-default-centre) over a new dedicated `graph` node. Tradeoffs: reuses proven pan/zoom + hit-testing + offline (no network layout deps) at the cost of no built-in force/radial solver \u2014 we compute deterministic ring positions ourselves (see sticky b) and feed them as fixed node coordinates, same as bublee's map does today. At 500+ nodes the existing canvas node is untested at that density; recommend capping the rendered graph to the topic-filtered subset (chip already in frame 1) rather than building a new engine node for this round. Color pick for individually-saved ARTICLES (depth 0): sage #6B8F71 \u2014 my own choice, not an existing wikipick token, chosen to read as cool/neutral against sepia bg #211912 and terracotta accents #e09a80/#7A2E1D. Composer widgets carry no per-widget color field today, so this palette is a spec note for the eventual graph renderer, not something drawn in this Moku frame itself."],r,q),A.y(["id","st_wsm_layout_rule","board",s,"x",470,"y",-260,"width",340,"text","(b) LAYOUT: deterministic radial rings per seed, NO physics/jitter \u2014 must read smooth on phone per the fleet's map-pan-must-be-smooth standard (pan must stay smooth regardless of data volume/layout complexity). A force-directed layout would recompute node positions every frame under drag, which is exactly what that standard rules out; fixed concentric rings (seed at center, ring1/ring2 at fixed radii, shared members interpolated to the midpoint between their seeds' centers) are computed once per topic-filter change, not per frame."],r,q),A.y(["id","st_wsm_data_model","board",s,"x",0,"y",780,"width",340,"text","(c) DATA MODEL: one DERIVED table/view built from `seeds` + `crawl_members` (depth, seed\u2192member edges, shared-member overlap per W16's unified seed model) \u2014 explicitly NO new persisted graph table. Node role (seed/article/layer1/layer2/shared) and ring position are computed at read time from existing rows; nothing new to keep in sync on save/delete/refcount."],r,q),A.y(["id","st_wsm_placement","board",s,"x",470,"y",780,"width",340,"text",'(d) PLACEMENT: a 5th nav destination "Map" in the drawer (alongside Home/Library/Saving offline/Topics), plus a "View on map" entry in a Topic\'s \u22ee menu that opens the map pre-filtered to that topic.'],r,q)],t.Z)}()
